  "description": "Plan 9.9 (X5.4) acceptance. A 0.15 m cube balanced on one corner by three body-axis reaction wheels: the plant is the hand-derived equation block library/CornerCube.jl (quaternion + body rates + relative wheel rates, m = 0.42 kg, Thcm = 3e-3, Thw = 6e-4), driven by three ElectricDrive motors (R = 1 Ohm, L = 0.1 mH, k = 0.0335, rotor 1e-6) and a 2 ms discrete LQR (library/CubeLQR.jl, +-12 V) whose gain K (3 x 8) comes from design/design.py (finite-difference linearisation of an independent numpy replica, reduced state [tilt(2), omega(3), wheel(3)], DARE on (A/rho, B/rho), rho = 1.0005). Start: 2 degrees off the vertical. The reference numbers are design.py's non-linear closed loop (Radau, ZOH, clamp). DEC-M5-3: cube-3d-mb / cube-3d-mb-soft are the same cube built from the M3 spatial stdlib (Spherical3D pivot with kt = 1e8 / 1e6 N/m, RigidBody3D cube and wheels, Revolute3D, ElectricDrive) under the same controller; the compare entries bound the difference by the pivot compliance and compare_scaling shows that the quasi-static part scales as 1/kt.",
